[2026-11-02 09:36:01.394] [RAW_JSON] {"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c713c17a-497f-4139-b1b4-d7abd5778b85","status":"SUCCESS","response":"**Vibe Forge** is a multi-provider vibe-coding web application and agent execution engine. \n\n### Architecture\nIt is built using **Hexagonal / Clean Architecture** so that new LLM providers or execution runners can be added with zero modifications to the core domain, application logic, or UI layers:\n\n1. **Pure Domain** (`project/backend/app/domain`): Core data models, state machines, typed errors, and ports (standard library only).\n2. **Application** (`project/backend/app/application`): Business logic and orchestration, including `ProviderRegistry`, `PromptLinter`, `AppSettings`, and execution coordination (no direct I/O).\n3. **App Infrastructure** (`project/backend/app/infrastructure`): Configuration loading (YAML/env with failure isolation and variable interpolation), workspace management, persistence, and eventing.\n4. **LLM Providers** (`project/backend/providers/providers`): A decoupled package that depends only on `app.domain`. It includes:\n   - **`kit/`**: Template-method `BaseAgentRunner` and HTTP streaming runners.\n   - **`adapters/`**: Isolated provider integrations (e.g., OpenRouter, Gemini, Anthropic, Antigravity, custom packages, and Fake adapters for testing).\n5. **Presentation** (`project/backend/app/api` \u0026 `project/web`): FastAPI REST/WebSocket backend endpoints paired with a React + Vite frontend UI.\n","duration_seconds":7.1854812,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":7871,"output_tokens":305,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":8176}}}
